<rml>
<head>
	<title>VaCuus M2 Interaction Demo</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="m2_demo.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
	<div id="m2-title">VaCuus M2 // INTERACTION DEMO</div>

	<!-- 1. BUTTONS. RCSS only, no script: :hover, :active and :focus each restyle
	     them, so a screenshot says which state the input path produced. The three
	     are in normal flow inside the panel rather than absolutely positioned,
	     because vacuus.M2Demo.Rects prints the rects the UI thread actually
	     published and guessing coordinates from RCSS is what that command exists
	     to replace. -->
	<div id="p-buttons">
		<div class="panel-title">1 &#183; BUTTONS :hover :active :focus</div>
		<button id="btn-a" class="m2-btn">ALPHA</button>
		<button id="btn-b" class="m2-btn">BRAVO</button>
		<button id="btn-c" class="m2-btn last">CHARLIE</button>
	</div>

	<!-- 2. WHEEL-SCROLLABLE LIST. #list-clip carries `vacuus-interactive`, and that
	     is load-bearing rather than decoration: the snapshot's predicate would not
	     otherwise cover the list BODY (a plain div with no tab-index and a tag RmlUi
	     ships no behaviour for), so SVaCuusWidget::OnMouseWheel would answer
	     Unhandled over the rows and the wheel would zoom the game camera instead of
	     scrolling the list. The scrollbar itself is covered without any marker --
	     `scrollbarvertical` is in the known-interactive tag list (controller
	     decision D8) -- which is what makes dragging it work.

	     NOT `tab-index: auto` for the same job: that would make the list focusable,
	     and a focused scroll container swallows the arrow keys into
	     ElementDocument's navigation instead of scrolling. -->
	<div id="p-list">
		<div class="panel-title">2 &#183; WHEEL-SCROLL LIST (drag the bar too)</div>
		<div id="list-clip" vacuus-interactive>
			<div class="row">01 PLASMA CELL</div>
			<div class="row alt">02 COOLANT FLASK</div>
			<div class="row">03 RIFLE SCOPE MK II</div>
			<div class="row alt">04 BREACHING CHARGE</div>
			<div class="row">05 FIELD RATION</div>
			<div class="row alt">06 SIGNAL FLARE</div>
			<div class="row">07 REPAIR KIT</div>
			<div class="row alt">08 NIGHT OPTIC</div>
			<div class="row">09 SMOKE CANISTER</div>
			<div class="row alt">10 STIM INJECTOR</div>
			<div class="row">11 ARMOUR PLATE</div>
			<div class="row alt">12 DATA SLATE</div>
			<div class="row">13 GRAPPLE LINE</div>
			<div class="row alt">14 THERMAL LANCE</div>
			<div class="row">15 SPARE MAGAZINE</div>
			<div class="row alt">16 WATER PURIFIER</div>
			<div class="row">17 RADIO BEACON</div>
			<div class="row alt">18 LOCK BYPASS</div>
			<div class="row">19 SALVAGE TORCH</div>
			<div class="row alt">20 SPENT CASING</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 3. TEXT INPUT. `type="text"` is what makes the rect carry
	     EVaCuusRectFlags::TextInput (controller decision D14a), so the click that
	     lands in it also activates the platform IME context -- on Linux there is
	     none, and typing goes OnKeyChar -> the queue -> Context::ProcessTextInput
	     instead (D16). maxlength is RmlUi's own attribute
	     (InputTypeText.cpp:45-47). -->
	<div id="p-input">
		<div class="panel-title">3 &#183; TEXT INPUT (type, Tab, Shift-Tab)</div>
		<input id="m2-input" type="text" maxlength="24"/>
		<div class="hint">Tab moves ALPHA -&gt; BRAVO -&gt; CHARLIE -&gt; this field</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 4. PASS-THROUGH. `vacuus-passthrough` is a PLAIN attribute and the match is
	     case-insensitive (VaCuusInteractiveSnapshot.cpp:40-41); lowercase is the
	     convention.

	     WHY #pass-zone IS `tab-index: auto` IN THE RCSS: pass-through is the ABSENCE
	     of coverage, never an occluder, so marking a region that was never
	     interactive proves nothing -- it would read as pass-through either way. This
	     zone would be reported (and focusable) on its own merits, and the attribute
	     is the only reason it is not. Delete the attribute and the clicks below stop
	     reaching the game; that is the before/after.

	     #pass-inner is a real <button>, i.e. interactive by tag, and it is inside the
	     marked subtree -- so it is pruned too. That is the subtree half of the rule. -->
	<div id="p-pass">
		<div class="panel-title">4 &#183; PASS-THROUGH (clicks reach the GAME)</div>
		<div id="pass-zone" vacuus-passthrough>
			<div id="pass-label">tab-index: auto + vacuus-passthrough</div>
			<button id="pass-inner">pruned with its parent</button>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
